    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1399">

                <pb facs="1746" n="1546" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 (Potsdam)/8–145</note>
                <head>No. 1399<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the French Minister of
                        Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bidault</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 677</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-01">August 1, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have just received telephonic
                        instructions<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1399-f1"/> from the Secretary of State
                    who is at Potsdam to convey to Your Excellency an invitation to the Government
                    of France to become a member of the Allied Commission on Reparations. My
                    Government trusts that the Government of France will be willing to accept this
                    invitation and will appoint a representative as soon as possible.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson
                                Caffery</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d1399-a1.xml" xpointer="d1399-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1399-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1399-f1-content">
                <p>A copy of the invitation enclosed with this note which is in the Central Files of
                    the Department of State (file No. 740.00119 EW/8–145), in which the names of the three Powers in the opening
                    sentence are all abbreviated, bears the following manuscript notation:
                    “Telephoned to Caffery. Will be delivered
                    at 5 p.m. Aug. 1???”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
